![](images/9e/9e2e705cf17a5dca362c23a23e4d10067ff4390a3f9464dddb6745d78986c02a.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is $x\\in [0,1].$ This means that $\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined outside this interval.\n\nTherefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-\\infty }\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(2x-1)$ is undefined."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184239 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4bcc5d54-e7fd-5be5-9d00-4240d03e21cb" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Limits at Infinity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa045d5-9683-533e-b3b9-383180919e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0aa045d5-9683-533e-b3b9-383180919e80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315174} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c61dd80-a3fe-57a0-9d9a-a6d5e5d6f81c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316766}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b99f3255-7a91-5700-9ad5-6321b83c8397" :question/math-academy-id "q-343225" :question/problem "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3):$ \n\n![](images/bb/bb49c052cabe12e8869270ab61b1de9e7f45b6acd6eaa9bc0d4c6892446a7cb6.png)\n\nThe domain of $\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3)$ is $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Moreover, from the graph, we see that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\,\\infty }(10\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2x+3))=(10\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})=5\\pi .\n$$"}]}
